OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%* ** %-,*,$%** %-& (,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAI was being treated for
OL,4,Adehydration - when suddenly I couldn't
OL,5,Amove
OL,6,
OL,7,FCarmel McConnellogue was in hospital,
OL,8,Fbeing treated by medical staff for
OL,9,Fdehydration, when she suddenly felt she
OL,10,Fcould no longer move her body.
OL,12,FShe said she could not speak or feel
OL,13,Fher face and "everything was numb".
OL,15,FInitial symptoms suggested
OL,16,FMcConnellogue might have had a stroke -
OL,17,Fbut an MRI scan confirmed that she had
OL,18,FFunctional Neurological Disorder (FND),
OL,19,Fmeaning there was was a problem with
OL,20,Fhow her brain received and sent
OL,21,Finformation to the rest of her body.
OL,23,APub: 22-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,413,410,260,120,0,100
